+# Why CVE-2024-29164 Is Not Applicable to HDF5 1.10.6 and Requires No Patching
+
+This document explains why **CVE-2024-29164** is a **false positive** when reported against **HDF5 v1.10.6** (Debian 11 bullseye), and confirms that the vulnerable code **does not exist** in this version, making any patching unnecessary.
+
+---
+
+## 📑 Table of Contents
+
+- [Overview: What Is HDF5?](#-overview-what-is-hdf5)
+
+- [Why CVE-2024-29164 Is Reported](#-why-cve-2024-29164-is-reported)
+
+- [Why This Issue Does Not Affect Target Version](#-why-this-issue-does-not-affect-target-version)
+
+- [Technical Analysis and Proof](#-technical-analysis-and-proof)
+
+- [Why This Is a False Positive](#-why-this-is-a-false-positive)
+
+- [Why You Must NOT Patch This Manually](#-why-you-must-not-patch-this-manually)
+
+- [Recommendations](#-recommendations)
+
+- [Summary](#-summary)
+
+- [References](#-references)
+
+---
+
+## 📌 Overview: What Is HDF5?
+
+HDF5 (Hierarchical Data Format version 5) is a high-performance data management and storage suite that is commonly used to:
+
+- Store and organize large amounts of scientific data
+
+- Handle complex data objects and metadata
+
+- Enable efficient I/O operations for multi-dimensional arrays
+
+- Support data portability across different computing platforms
+
+Because HDF5 processes external data files and is used in scientific computing environments, it is frequently flagged by security scanners for potential vulnerabilities.
+
+---
+
+## ⚠️ Why CVE-2024-29164 Is Reported
+
+Security scanners report **CVE-2024-29164** based on:
+
+- Static vulnerability metadata from NVD and security advisories
+
+- Package name and broad version range matching (HDF5 "through 1.14.3")
+
+- Advisory data that does not evaluate actual source code presence
+
+- Lack of granularity in vulnerability version tracking
+
+As a result, scanners flag **HDF5 v1.10.6** without verifying whether the **vulnerable function actually exists** in this version.
+
+---
+
+## ✅ Why This Issue Does Not Affect Target Version
+
+The vulnerability described in **CVE-2024-29164** is **not present** in HDF5 v1.10.6.
+
+Key facts:
+
+- The vulnerable function `H5R__decode_heap` was **introduced in HDF5 1.12.0** as part of the new H5R2 reference API rewrite
+
+- HDF5 v1.10.6 uses the **legacy reference API** which does not contain this function
+
+- The target version is **2 major releases older** than when the vulnerability was introduced
+
+- The vulnerable code path **does not exist** in the installed version
+
+**Conclusion:**  
+
+The installed version is **not affected by this vulnerability**, and no remediation is required.
+
+---
+
+## 🔍 Technical Analysis and Proof
+
+### 🔹 Vulnerability Details
+
+| Attribute | Value |
+|-----------|-------|
+| CVE ID | CVE-2024-29164 |
+| CVSS v3 Score | 9.8 (CRITICAL) |
+| CWE | CWE-121 (Stack-based Buffer Overflow) |
+| Affected Component | src/H5Rint.c |
+| Affected Function | H5R__decode_heap |
+| Vulnerability Type | Stack buffer overflow |
+
+### 🔹 Vulnerability Description
+
+The vulnerability exists in HDF5's reference decoding functionality. A stack buffer overflow in `H5R__decode_heap` can result in the corruption of the instruction pointer, causing denial of service or potential code execution. This function is part of the new H5R2 reference API introduced in HDF5 1.12.0.
+
+### 🔹 Version Timeline
+
+| Version | Status |
+|---------|--------|
+| HDF5 1.10.x | Legacy reference API - **NOT AFFECTED** |
+| HDF5 1.12.0 | New H5R2 API introduced - **VULNERABLE** |
+| HDF5 1.14.3 | Still vulnerable |
+| HDF5 1.14.4 | **FIXED** |
+
+### 🔹 Upstream Fix Details
+
+| Attribute | Value |
+|-----------|-------|
+| Fix Commit | 136739b37a9e1ecefe83883f0f422d283ae497e5 |
+| Fix Description | Fix stack buffer overflow in H5R__decode_heap |
